      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Sure I can wrap this function in bssl_avf so that pvmfw doesn\u0027t need to depend on bssl_ffi anymore.\n\nSGTM\n\n\u003e But we probably don\u0027t need to track the calling since it\u0027s safe to call it multiple times [1]. wdyt?\n\nI meant track it so that it\u0027s still called once before any other BSSL function; are you suggesting `bssl_avf` would call `CRYPTO_library_init` every time it calls a BSSL function? That would provide the encapsulation but I\u0027m not sure how expensive unnecessary calls are (and, if inexpensive today, if our Rust wrapper should be built on that assumption)? Anyway, any solution moving this to `bssl_avf` is better for correctness of clients, IMO.",
