      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Also the bssl team does recommend to use the two `*_randnonce` APIs.\n\nI\u0027m out of my realm here but I vaguely remember discussions about avoiding `_randnonce` and generating the nonce ourselves (to pass it to the non-`randnonce` functions): could you confirm that you actually meant \"does\" (not \"does not\") in the above and/or if you think there would be value in doing so?\n\nLeaving this comment thread resolved as it\u0027s out-of-scope for this CL.",
